---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About McFuzzySquirrel's Playground and learning by building in public."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <PageHeader
      kicker="About the workshop"
      title="Learning out loud, one build at a time"
      intro="McFuzzySquirrel's Playground is my place to build in public: a friendly workshop for AI experiments, useful tools, creative prototypes, and the lessons that come with making them."
    />

    <div class="about-layout">
      <div class="about-copy prose">
        <p>
          I&rsquo;m Doug McCusker. I learn by turning questions into working software, then sharing the process &mdash;
          not just the polished result. Here you&rsquo;ll find what worked, what didn&rsquo;t, and what I learned along
          the way.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most of my projects explore AI agents, practical developer tools, local-first workflows, and creative
          technology. Some are useful answers to real problems; others are experiments pursued out of curiosity. All
          are part of learning by doing.
        </p>

        <h2>How this workshop runs</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Build in public.</strong> Notes go up while the idea is still warm, not after it is framed.</li>
          <li><strong>Show the decisions.</strong> The interesting part is usually why something changed.</li>
          <li><strong>Keep it useful.</strong> A tool earns its bench space by solving a real problem.</li>
          <li><strong>Stay curious.</strong> &ldquo;I wonder if&hellip;&rdquo; is a valid starting point.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Explore</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Browse <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> for a curated look at what I&rsquo;m building.</li>
          <li>Read the <a href="/blog/">Blog</a> for the stories, decisions, and discoveries behind the work.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>GitHub: <a href={SITE.github} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">McFuzzySquirrel</a></li>
          <li>LinkedIn: <a href={SITE.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Doug McCusker</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p>If a project sparks a question or gives you an idea to try, I&rsquo;d be glad to hear about it.</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="about-portrait">
        <img
          src="/assets/images/2026-08-10-the-unexpected-journey/inception.png"
          alt="A curious squirrel watching a spinning top on a workbench"
          width="1536"
          height="1024"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption><span class="bench-tag">Curious by default</span> Most ideas start as a what-if.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
